# Project Intelligence

## Overview

This project uses the **BMAD Method v6** for structured planning and development,
orchestrated via **Claude Code Agent Teams** for parallel execution.

**Autonomy principle:** Agents operate autonomously through all validation,
review, and improvement cycles. They apply recommended improvements directly
without waiting for human selection. They walk through every element of every
artifact exhaustively. The AI Development Lifecycle (AI/DLC) runs from idea
to production deployment in a single conversation. The only human checkpoint
is **production validation** after deployment. Agents seek clarity when they
detect ambiguity, but do not block on human approval at phase transitions.
Token cost and cycle time are secondary to thoroughness.

**Continuous flow:** The pipeline runs as a continuous, uninterrupted
flow. There are exactly THREE points where agents stop and wait for
human input: (a) genuine ambiguity requiring clarification, (b) the
Production Validation Checkpoint, and (c) the retro commentary prompt.
At ALL other times — between sub-skills, within sub-skills, during
long validation cycles, during large artifact generation, during
multi-pass adversarial review — agents keep working. Do not stop and
wait for human input. Do not ask if you should continue. Do not treat
a natural break point within a step as a stopping point. If you are
not at one of the three pause points, you are not done — keep going.
**Show your work** — output sub-skill results (party mode debates,
adversarial findings, elicitation probes) to the conversation so the
human can observe, then immediately continue to the next action.
Outputting results and continuing is correct; outputting results and
waiting for a response is stalling.

**Handoff is not a fifth pause point.** When the user requests
handoff to a new conversation, the agent finalizes the pipeline
snapshot, outputs a pasteable resume prompt, and ENDS the current
session — it does not pause and wait. The new conversation is a
separate session that resumes from the snapshot. The yellow- and
red-threshold context reminders are one-line outputs, not pauses —
the agent continues immediately after issuing them. The four pause
points are: ambiguity resolution, Production Validation Checkpoint,
retro commentary prompt, and post-compact verification turn (see
"Post-Compact Recovery Protocol" below).

Every planning artifact goes through **Party Mode** (multi-agent debate),
**Advanced Elicitation** (probe until zero ambiguity), and **Adversarial
Review** (multi-pass, apply all fixes autonomously between passes).

Every implementation artifact goes through a **three-gate validation**:
Code Review (opus), QA functional validation (sonnet), and Story Validation.

