## Model Strategy

| Role          | Model  | Effort | Rationale                                              |
|---------------|--------|--------|--------------------------------------------------------|
| Lead          | opus   | high   | Orchestration, validation cycles, gate checks          |
| PM            | opus   | high   | Requirements elicitation and edge-case analysis        |
| Architect     | opus   | high   | System design, tradeoff evaluation, ADRs               |
| Dev           | sonnet | medium | Implementation is high-volume, well-scoped by stories  |
| QA            | sonnet | medium | Test validation is pattern-matching against criteria   |
| Code Reviewer | opus   | high   | Cross-cutting review needs architectural context       |

<!-- Model strategy note: The table above assumes access to both opus
     and sonnet. If your environment only has sonnet (e.g., Bedrock
     without opus access), /ai-dlc-setup will set all roles to sonnet.
     Effort levels (high for planning, medium for implementation)
     compensate partially for using the same model across all roles. -->

Effort levels are set via skill frontmatter (lead) and role files
(teammates). Planning roles use `high` for deeper reasoning during
validation cycles. Implementation roles use `medium` for efficient
throughput on well-scoped work.

